      {
        "position": 5,
        "title": "Bright, Lightweight, and Feature-Packed Headlamp for Camping and Outdoor Use",
        "text": "I’ve been using this headlamp for camping and general outdoor tasks, and it’s been a solid performer overall. The 500-lumen output is genuinely bright, especially on the spotlight and mixed beam modes. It’s more than enough for night hiking, setting up camp, or working around the car or campsite after dark. I also appreciate having the red light and red flashing modes, which are useful for preserving night vision or signaling when needed.The built-in 2200mAh battery has been very convenient. Charging over USB-C makes it easy to top up from a power bank, car charger, or wall adapter, and battery life has been good for my use. I haven’t come close to running it dry during a weekend trip, even at lower brightness levels. The stepless dimming is a nice touch since you can dial in exactly how much light you want instead of being stuck with preset levels.One of my favorite features is the motion sensor. Being able to turn the light on and off with a simple wave is surprisingly useful, especially when wearing gloves or when your hands are dirty. It works reliably and can be turned off when you don’t need it, which I appreciate.The headlamp is lightweight and comfortable to wear for extended periods. At 95 grams, it doesn’t feel front-heavy, and the adjustable elastic band holds it securely whether I’m walking, jogging, or bending down to work on something. The IPX6 waterproof rating also gives peace of mind. I’ve used it in the rain without any issues, and it feels durable enough for regular outdoor use.Overall, this is a well-designed, feature-rich headlamp that balances brightness, comfort, and practicality. It’s easy to use, rechargeable, lightweight, and versatile enough for camping, hiking, running, and everyday tasks around the house or garage.",
